<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cambodian People's Party</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kampuchean People's Revolutionary Party, CPP</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kampuchean People's Revolutionary Party was the ruling communist party of the People's Republic of Kampuchea, set up after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a> in 1979 and claiming descent from the party founded in 1951. Led by former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> Rouge cadres such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heng-samrin">Heng Samrin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hun-sen">Hun Sen</a>, it ruled as the sole legal party under Vietnamese protection. In 1991 it abandoned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marxism-leninism">Marxism–Leninism</a> and renamed itself the Cambodian People's Party, which has dominated Cambodian politics since.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cambodian-peoples-party.jpg" alt="Cambodian People's Party" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zachary Harden · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Cambodian_People%27s_Party.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
